scope: |
  SSC3-14b — varargs, `def f(xs: T*)`. `Dataset.of` is called 35 times in the corpus and
  `std/mapreduce/dataset.ssc:21` declares `def of[T](items: T*)`, which is what blocks the module;
  `std/ui/data.ssc:43` is the other declarer.

  THE PLAN IS HERE AND NOT IN SPRINT.md BECAUSE `v3/SPRINT.md` IS CLAIMED by
  `bench-b4-three-version-table`, taken 2026-08-14T07:17Z — live, not stale. Write-before-do is
  satisfied by this field: it is in git, before the edit. SSC3-14b's entry in SPRINT.md gets
  corrected when that path frees; posted in the room so its holder can do it first.

  THE RECORDED DIAGNOSIS IN SPRINT.md IS WRONG AND MUST NOT BE ACTED ON. It says "the star is eaten
  below the parser — in the lexer or in `alphabet/src/Alphabet.scala`" and tells the next reader to
  dump tokens. The dump was taken, against the built kernel classes: `def total(xs: Int*)` lexes as
  `TId(Int) TOp(*) TPunct())` — the star is a real token at 1:18 and the lexer never touches it.

  WHAT IS ACTUALLY TRUE, and it is a two-front pair. `SSC3_FRONT=v3` refuses at exactly 1:18,
  `expected ')', found *` — v3's own `skipType` has no case for the star. The DEFAULT front takes
  the file, because `v3/.jars/uniml.cp` exists and `Front.default` is uniml when it is registered;
  uniml then DISCARDS the star at `ScalaSpike.scala:708` inside `skipTypeTail`, deliberately and
  with a comment saying so. So `Param.tpe` arrives as `Int` and the vararg fact is gone before
  `UniFront` can see it. My two earlier attempts edited `v3/src/Parser.scala` — the front that does
  not compile it — which is the same trap `v3-extension-in-trait` recorded one task earlier.

  THE STAR RIDES IN THE TYPE TEXT, no new field on any AST. `SpikeTyped.slots` already REWRITES
  `tpe.text` for `def.typearg` (`Show` + `A` -> `Show[A]`), so appending `*` there is the shape the
  file already has; `UniFront.scala:429` carries `p.tpe.map(_.text)` unchanged and needs no edit,
  which is why it is not in `paths`; v3's own `typeTextOf` reassembles the type from its tokens and
  produces `Int*` for free once `skipType` stops refusing. `Lower` then keys on
  `ps.last.tpe.exists(_.endsWith("*"))` at ONE site.

  FOUR EDITS. (1) `ScalaSpike.scala`, in the param loop only, capture the star as a `def.vararg`
  leaf BEFORE `skipTypeTail` gets it — the roled-leaf precedent that file states for `def.byname`,
  and leaving `skipTypeTail`'s own case alone so its other callers (return types, patterns) are
  untouched. (2) `SpikeTyped.slots`, one arm appending `*` to the type it follows. (3)
  `Parser.skipType`, accept a trailing star so v3's own front stops refusing. (4) `Lower`,
  `collectVarargs` BEFORE `fillDefaults` and `checkArity` — the order matters, the arity check
  legitimately rejects `passes 3, it takes 1` until the tail is collected.

  SEMANTICS READ OFF THE TREE, NOT CHOSEN: `std/ui/data.ssc:43` is
  `def tableRow(cells: TkNode*): List[TkNode] = cells.toList`, so the body already treats a vararg
  parameter as an ordinary `List[T]`. At Tier 0 `T*` IS `List[T]` and only the call site changes.

  RISK, and it is why uniml is in scope at all: `Param.tpe` text feeds instance resolution
  (`resolveGivenArgs` unifies type TEXT). A parameter typed `Int*` simply matches no instance, which
  is correct, but the consumers get checked before the edit rather than after. Touching a SHARED
  subsystem, so uniml's own test suite runs too — a green v3 corpus is not evidence for uniml.

  MEASUREMENT: N with floors DIFF 3 and CRASH 9, against the same tree minus exactly this change.
  v3's gates do not cover the corpus, so gates green is not evidence that N held.

  MEASURED 2026-08-14, AND THE MOTIVATION ABOVE DID NOT MATERIALISE. N is 212/369 with the change
  and 212/369 without it — PASS, DIFF, UNSUPPORTED, CRASH and LANE-EXCL all identical, so varargs
  delivered ZERO new passes. The reason is not a mystery and is worth writing down: the prelude's
  own `object Dataset` declares `of` with SIXTEEN DEFAULTED PARAMETERS, which is a workaround for
  exactly this missing feature, so every `dataset-*` case already passed through it. And
  `std/mapreduce/dataset.ssc` is an `extern object` — declarations with no implementation, so its
  names are host gaps on v3 and would refuse even with the parse fixed. "35 call sites blocked" was
  a LOWER BOUND on the blocker and never a forecast of the yield; a refusal short-circuits, so what
  it hides can be another refusal.

  WHAT IT DID DELIVER, measured by the gate built to see it: `front-capability-gate` turns RED in
  the GOOD direction, reporting four rows that NO LONGER DIVERGE — `std-os`, `std-os-doc-import`,
  `std-os-readline` (all on `std/os.ssc:61`, `extern def pathJoin(parts: String*)`) and
  `cluster-connect`. Those were declared `accepted only by uniml`: one language answering two ways
  depending on whether `v3/.jars/uniml.cp` happened to exist. That is the result of this change,
  and it is a front-agreement result rather than an N result.

  WIDENED 2026-08-14 to `v3/front-capability-gate.sh`, BEFORE the edit. The gate is
  self-maintaining and demands its own declared list be corrected in the commit that fixes a row,
  which is the only reason it is touched: four names come out of KNOWN_uniml, nothing else changes.
